,"anchor":"overview","level":2,"text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"In fact if it seems some rules are missing, or weight are not managed, if the font family only is returned","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the user has an higher probability to use the expected font. Because if a mashup of family name and weight is returned","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"it can produce a PostScript identifier not available, so not usable, so implying a fallback to default system font like "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"San Francisco","type":"text"}]},{"text":".","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Because PostScript identifiers in most of cases do not have whitespaces, remove them.","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","code":["    \/\/ Given a dictionary with one value","    let myDict: PostScriptFontNamesMap = [PSFNMK(\"Arial\", Font.Weight.bold): \"Aria-BoldMT\"]","","    \/\/ The given value is returned if the key exists","    let keyExists = myDict[PSFNMK(\"Arial\", Font.Weight.bold)] \/\/ Arial-BoldMT","","    \/\/ But if the key does not exist, the only the key is returned","    let keyDoesNotExist = myDict[PSFNMK(\"Luciole\", Font.Weight.bold)] \/\/ Luciole"],"type":"codeListing"}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/OUDSFoundations\/documentation\/OUDSFoundations","doc:\/\/OUDSFoundations\/documentation\/OUDSFoundations\/Swift","doc:\/\/OUDSFoundations\/documentation\/OUDSFoundations\/Swift\/Dictionary"]]},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"If there is no value for the given "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"key"},{"type":"text","text":", returns the description of this key,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"i.e.font family name without the font weight in the end and without whitespaces."}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/oudsfoundations\/swift\/dictionary\/subscript(orkey:)"]}],"references":{"doc://OU